The latest MSTest is **4.2.3**. Going from 3.8.0 → 4.x is a major version bump with several breaking changes. Here's what affects **your code specifically**:

### 1. `[ExpectedException]` is removed (build error)
This is your biggest issue. Both test methods using `[ExpectedException]` will fail to compile. Replace with `Assert.ThrowsExactly`:

```csharp
// Before
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}

// After
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

### 2. `Assert.IsTrue(true)` triggers MSTEST0032 (warning)
This analyzer was promoted from Info → Warning in v4. Your `Validate_ValidInput_Succeeds` test will produce a warning.

### 3. No parallelization attribute triggers MSTEST0001 (warning)
Also promoted to Warning in v4. Add `[assembly: Parallelize]` or `[assembly: DoNotParallelize]` to suppress.

### Other v4 breaking changes (not in your code, but FYI):
- `TestMethodAttribute.Execute` → `ExecuteAsync` (custom attributes)
- `ClassCleanupBehavior` enum removed
- `TestContext.Properties` is now `IDictionary<string, object>`
- `TestTimeout` enum removed
- `Assert` format-string overloads (`message, params object[]`) simplified
- Minimum TFM is .NET 8 (you're fine)

Full migration guide: https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/core/testing/unit-testing-mstest-migration-v3-v4

Would you like me to apply these fixes to your project?
